    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0456" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/7–2049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-20">July 20,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received July 20—5:07 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>300. Press carries announcement of creation of office of Generalissimo in Taipei
                    under Chief Secretary Huang Shao-ku. Five sections: <pb facs="0457" n="447"
                        xml:id="pg447"/> Party and political sections under Ku Cheng-kang; foreign
                    section under Wang Shih-chieh; finance section under O. K. Yui; military section
                    under General Wang Tung-yuan; secretariat under Professor Chang Chi-yun.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; repeated OffEmb Canton 130.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
